    "answer": "The claim is defined as the constant `CUSTOMER_NUMBER_CLAIM = 'customer_number'` in `apps/api/src/oauth/customerIdentity.ts`. In that file, `identityFromClaims` reads the claim and turns it into a `CustomerIdentity` of `{userId, customerNumber}`. If `sub` is missing or the claim isn't a non-empty string, it returns null. The stand-in login in `apps/api/src/dummyPortal/dummyIssuer.ts` imports the constant and writes the claim into its tokens. A code comment says the real login's claim name will replace this one (RD-5). ADR-001 says the same thing.",
